{"type":"message","id":"88dc6cd4","parentId":"75b7b49e","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:22.623Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ah, the API returns \"Unauthorized\" when calling directly with curl. That's because the frontend likely sends an auth token. But when AleX uses the UI through the browser, the auth token is included. The 500 error suggests something else is wrong.\n\nLet me look at the projects route and service to understand what data the API expects and what might be causing the 500 error. Also, let me look at the frontend's ProjectsPage to see what data it sends.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_eZgbsLVNCp8wn9QSRUpX6929","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/modules/projects/projects.routes.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_bO3Pv7ksRONRjiagdZZl3932","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/modules/projects/projects.service.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":236,"output":220,"cacheRead":37760,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38216,"cost":{"input":0.00041064000000000004,"output":0.0007656000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0054751999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00665144}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840454310,"responseId":"a0ede784-107f-47ac-98de-1c1baf587371"}}
{"type":"message","id":"dbd48def","parentId":"88dc6cd4","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:25.109Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_eZgbsLVNCp8wn9QSRUpX6929","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { FastifyInstance } from 'fastify';\nimport { CreateProjectBody, UpdateProjectBody, StageChangeBody, SubStatusChangeBody, ProjectQuery } from './projects.schema.js';\nimport * as projectsService from './projects.service.js';\n\nexport default async function projectsRoutes(fastify: FastifyInstance) {\n  fastify.get('/', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const query = ProjectQuery.parse(request.query);\n    const data = await projectsService.list(query);\n    return { data };\n  });\n\n  fastify.get('/:id', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const { id } = request.params as { id: string };\n    const data = await projectsService.getById(id);\n    return { data };\n  });\n\n  fastify.post('/', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request, reply) => {\n    const body = CreateProjectBody.parse(request.body);\n    const data = await projectsService.create(body);\n    return reply.status(201).send({ data });\n  });\n\n  fastify.put('/:id', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const { id } = request.params as { id: string };\n    const body = UpdateProjectBody.parse(request.body);\n    const data = await projectsService.update(id, body);\n    return { data };\n  });\n\n  fastify.patch('/:id/stage', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const { id } = request.params as { id: string };\n    const { stage } = StageChangeBody.parse(request.body);\n    const data = await projectsService.changeStage(id, stage);\n    return { data };\n  });\n\n  fastify.patch('/:id/substatus', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const { id } = request.params as { id: string };\n    const { subStatus } = SubStatusChangeBody.parse(request.body);\n    const data = await projectsService.changeSubStatus(id, subStatus);\n    return { data };\n  });\n\n  fastify.delete('/:id', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const { id } = request.params as { id: string };\n    const data = await projectsService.remove(id);\n    return { data };\n  });\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840465109}}
{"type":"message","id":"81069353","parentId":"dbd48def","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:25.109Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_bO3Pv7ksRONRjiagdZZl3932","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { prisma } from '../../lib/prisma.js';\nimport { NotFoundError, ValidationError } from '../../lib/errors.js';\nimport type { CreateProjectBody, UpdateProjectBody } from './projects.schema.js';\nimport { PROJECT_STAGES, PROJECT_SUB_STATUSES } from './projects.schema.js';\n\nexport async function list(query: { stage?: string; peopleId?: string; search?: string }) {\n  const where: Record<string, unknown> = {};\n  if (query.stage) where.stage = query.stage;\n  if (query.peopleId) where.peopleId = query.peopleId;\n  if (query.search) {\n    where.OR = [\n      { name: { contains: query.search } },\n      { description: { contains: query.search } },\n    ];\n  }\n  return prisma.project.findMany({\n    where,\n    include: { people: true, conversations: true },\n    orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },\n  });\n}\n\nexport async function getById(id: string) {\n  const project = await prisma.project.findUnique({\n    where: { id },\n    include: {\n      people: true,\n      conversations: { orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' } },\n      files: true,\n      requirements: { orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' } },\n      milestones: { orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' } },\n      collaborators: true,\n      plans: { orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' } },\n      analytics: { orderBy: { generatedAt: 'desc' } },\n    },\n  });\n  if (!project) throw new NotFoundError('Project');\n  return project;\n}\n\nexport async function create(data: CreateProjectBody) {\n  const project = await prisma.project.create({ data });\n  if (data.peopleId) {\n    await prisma.activity.create({\n      data: {\n        peopleId: data.peopleId,\n        projectId: project.id,\n        type: 'created',\n        description: `Project \"${data.name}\" created`,\n        metadata: JSON.stringify({ stage: data.stage }),\n      },\n    });\n  }\n  return project;\n}\n\nexport async function update(id: string, data: UpdateProjectBody) {\n  await getById(id);\n  return prisma.project.update({ where: { id }, data });\n}\n\nexport async function changeStage(id: string, stage: string) {\n  if (!PROJECT_STAGES.includes(stage as typeof PROJECT_STAGES[number])) {\n    throw new ValidationError(`Invalid stage. Must be one of: ${PROJECT_STAGES.join(', ')}`);\n  }\n  await getById(id);\n  // Clear subStatus when moving between top-level stages\n  const updated = await prisma.project.update({ where: { id }, data: { stage, subStatus: null } });\n  await prisma.activity.create({\n    data: {\n      projectId: id,\n      type: 'stage_changed',\n      description: `Project stage changed to ${stage}`,\n      metadata: JSON.stringify({ newStage: stage }),\n    },\n  });\n  return updated;\n}\n\nexport async function changeSubStatus(id: string, subStatus: string) {\n  const project = await getById(id);\n  const validSubs = PROJECT_SUB_STATUSES[project.stage];\n  if (!validSubs || !validSubs.includes(subStatus as typeof validSubs[number])) {\n    const valid = validSubs ? validSubs.join(', ') : '(no sub-statuses for this stage)';\n    throw new ValidationError(`Invalid sub-status for stage \"${project.stage}\". Valid options: ${valid}`);\n  }\n  const updated = await prisma.project.update({ where: { id }, data: { subStatus } });\n  await prisma.activity.create({\n    data: {\n      projectId: id,\n      type: 'stage_changed',\n      description: `Sub-status changed to ${subStatus}`,\n      metadata: JSON.stringify({ newSubStatus: subStatus }),\n    },\n  });\n  return updated;\n}\n\nexport async function remove(id: string) {\n  await getById(id);\n  await prisma.project.delete({ where: { id } });\n  return { success: true };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840465109}}
{"type":"message","id":"c12aa447","parentId":"81069353","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:38.598Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me look at the schema to understand what fields `CreateProjectBody` expects, and also look at the frontend's `ProjectsPage.tsx` to see what data it's sending. I also need to look at the Prisma schema to check if there's a mismatch.\n\nLet me also check how the 500 error is being caught in the routes - the `.parse()` call on the Zod schema would throw a Zod error if validation fails, but Fastify might not be catching it properly, leading to a 500 instead of a 400.\n\nLet me look at:\n1. The schema definition for CreateProjectBody\n2. The frontend's ProjectsPage to see what it sends\n3. The error handling in the API\n4. The Prisma schema to see the Project model","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ceRKUxtemxoSvKQMlldp5392","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src -name \"projects.schema.ts\" -exec cat {} \\; 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_7JUmue8vKDjhGAzCOViB7683","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api -name \"schema.prisma\" -exec cat {} \\; 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_8RsIp3ikOvud0wc7Cz0D3403","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-ui/src -name \"ProjectsPage.tsx\" -exec cat {} \\; 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1484,"output":417,"cacheRead":38144,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40045,"cost":{"input":0.00258216,"output":0.00145116,"cacheRead":0.005530879999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.009564199999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840465110,"responseId":"8d7d7f53-8594-456e-ab97-3d0e353f3408"}}
{"type":"message","id":"05f51195","parentId":"c12aa447","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:42.059Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_ceRKUxtemxoSvKQMlldp5392","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { z } from 'zod/v4';\n\nexport const PROJECT_STAGES = [\n  'Contact', 'Opportunity', 'Proposal', 'Implementation',\n  'Onboarding', 'Live', 'Validated',\n] as const;\n\n/** Sub-statuses per stage: which sub-status values are valid for each stage */\nexport const PROJECT_SUB_STATUSES: Record<string, readonly string[]> = {\n  Proposal: [\n    'Proposal Preparation',\n    'Proposal Accepted',\n    'Waiting for Contract & Payment',\n  ] as const,\n};\n\nexport const CreateProjectBody = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(1),\n  description: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  stage: z.string().default('Contact'),\n  subStatus: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  value: z.number().positive().optional().nullable(),\n  peopleId: z.string(),\n});\n\nexport const UpdateProjectBody = CreateProjectBody.partial();\n\nexport const StageChangeBody = z.object({\n  stage: z.enum(PROJECT_STAGES),\n});\n\nexport const SubStatusChangeBody = z.object({\n  subStatus: z.string(),\n});\n\nexport const ProjectQuery = z.object({\n  stage: z.string().optional(),\n  peopleId: z.string().optional(),\n  search: z.string().optional(),\n});\n\nexport type CreateProjectBody = z.infer<typeof CreateProjectBody>;\nexport type UpdateProjectBody = z.infer<typeof UpdateProjectBody>;"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2623,"aggregated":"import { z } from 'zod/v4';\n\nexport const PROJECT_STAGES = [\n  'Contact', 'Opportunity', 'Proposal', 'Implementation',\n  'Onboarding', 'Live', 'Validated',\n] as const;\n\n/** Sub-statuses per stage: which sub-status values are valid for each stage */\nexport const PROJECT_SUB_STATUSES: Record<string, readonly string[]> = {\n  Proposal: [\n    'Proposal Preparation',\n    'Proposal Accepted',\n    'Waiting for Contract & Payment',\n  ] as const,\n};\n\nexport const CreateProjectBody = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(1),\n  description: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  stage: z.string().default('Contact'),\n  subStatus: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  value: z.number().positive().optional().nullable(),\n  peopleId: z.string(),\n});\n\nexport const UpdateProjectBody = CreateProjectBody.partial();\n\nexport const StageChangeBody = z.object({\n  stage: z.enum(PROJECT_STAGES),\n});\n\nexport const SubStatusChangeBody = z.object({\n  subStatus: z.string(),\n});\n\nexport const ProjectQuery = z.object({\n  stage: z.string().optional(),\n  peopleId: z.string().optional(),\n  search: z.string().optional(),\n});\n\nexport type CreateProjectBody = z.infer<typeof CreateProjectBody>;\nexport type UpdateProjectBody = z.infer<typeof UpdateProjectBody>;","cwd":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840482059}}
{"type":"message","id":"efe8b088","parentId":"05f51195","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:42.059Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_7JUmue8vKDjhGAzCOViB7683","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"generator client {\n  provider = \"prisma-client\"\n  output   = \"../generated/prisma\"\n}\n\ndatasource db {\n  provider = \"sqlite\"\n}\n\nmodel User {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  email     String   @unique\n  password  String\n  name      String\n  role      String   @default(\"admin\")\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel People {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  type      String   @default(\"client\")\n  name      String\n  email     String?\n  phone     String?\n  company   String?\n  stage     String   @default(\"Contact\")\n  notes     String?\n  tags      String   @default(\"\")\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n\n  projects   Project[]\n  activities Activity[]\n}\n\nmodel Project {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  name        String\n  description String?\n  stage       String   @default(\"Contact\")\n  subStatus   String?\n  value       Float?\n  peopleId    String\n  people      People   @relation(fields: [peopleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n\n  conversations Conversation[]\n  files         ProjectFile[]\n  requirements  Requirement[]\n  milestones    Milestone[]\n  collaborators Collaborator[]\n  plans         ProjectPlan[]\n  analytics     AnalyticsRecord[]\n}\n\nmodel Conversation {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  channel   String   @default(\"manual\")\n  direction String   @default(\"inbound\")\n  subject   String?\n  content   String\n  metadata  String?\n  sentiment Float?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel ProjectFile {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  name      String\n  url       String\n  type      String   @default(\"file\")\n  mimeType  String?\n  size      Int?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel Requirement {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId   String\n  project     Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title       String\n  description String?\n  category    String   @default(\"requirement\")\n  status      String   @default(\"open\")\n  priority    String   @default(\"medium\")\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel Milestone {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId   String\n  project     Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title       String\n  description String?\n  dueDate     DateTime?\n  status      String   @default(\"pending\")\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel Collaborator {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  name      String\n  email     String?\n  phone     String?\n  role      String?\n  notes     String?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel ProjectPlan {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title     String\n  content   String\n  version   Int      @default(1)\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel AnalyticsRecord {\n  id              String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId       String\n  project         Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sentimentScore  Float?\n  alignmentScore  Float?\n  healthScore     Float?\n  engagementScore Float?\n  rawData         String?\n  generatedAt     DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel Activity {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  peopleId    String?\n  people      People?  @relation(fields: [peopleId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  projectId   String?\n  type        String   @default(\"created\")\n  description String\n  metadata    String?\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2276,"aggregated":"generator client {\n  provider = \"prisma-client\"\n  output   = \"../generated/prisma\"\n}\n\ndatasource db {\n  provider = \"sqlite\"\n}\n\nmodel User {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  email     String   @unique\n  password  String\n  name      String\n  role      String   @default(\"admin\")\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel People {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  type      String   @default(\"client\")\n  name      String\n  email     String?\n  phone     String?\n  company   String?\n  stage     String   @default(\"Contact\")\n  notes     String?\n  tags      String   @default(\"\")\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n\n  projects   Project[]\n  activities Activity[]\n}\n\nmodel Project {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  name        String\n  description String?\n  stage       String   @default(\"Contact\")\n  subStatus   String?\n  value       Float?\n  peopleId    String\n  people      People   @relation(fields: [peopleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n\n  conversations Conversation[]\n  files         ProjectFile[]\n  requirements  Requirement[]\n  milestones    Milestone[]\n  collaborators Collaborator[]\n  plans         ProjectPlan[]\n  analytics     AnalyticsRecord[]\n}\n\nmodel Conversation {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  channel   String   @default(\"manual\")\n  direction String   @default(\"inbound\")\n  subject   String?\n  content   String\n  metadata  String?\n  sentiment Float?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel ProjectFile {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  name      String\n  url       String\n  type      String   @default(\"file\")\n  mimeType  String?\n  size      Int?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel Requirement {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId   String\n  project     Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title       String\n  description String?\n  category    String   @default(\"requirement\")\n  status      String   @default(\"open\")\n  priority    String   @default(\"medium\")\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel Milestone {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId   String\n  project     Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title       String\n  description String?\n  dueDate     DateTime?\n  status      String   @default(\"pending\")\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel Collaborator {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  name      String\n  email     String?\n  phone     String?\n  role      String?\n  notes     String?\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel ProjectPlan {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId String\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  title     String\n  content   String\n  version   Int      @default(1)\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel AnalyticsRecord {\n  id              String   @id @default(cuid())\n  projectId       String\n  project         Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sentimentScore  Float?\n  alignmentScore  Float?\n  healthScore     Float?\n  engagementScore Float?\n  rawData         String?\n  generatedAt     DateTime @default(now())\n}\n\nmodel Activity {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  peopleId    String?\n  people      People?  @relation(fields: [peopleId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  projectId   String?\n  type        String   @default(\"created\")\n  description String\n  metadata    String?\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n}","cwd":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840482059}}
{"type":"message","id":"caec131d","parentId":"efe8b088","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:34:42.060Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_8RsIp3ikOvud0wc7Cz0D3403","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import React, { useState } from 'react'\nimport { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom'\nimport { useProjects, useCreateProject, useChangeProjectStage, useDeleteProject } from '../hooks/useProjects'\nimport { usePeople } from '../hooks/usePeople'\nimport { Button } from '../components/ui/button'\nimport { Input } from '../components/ui/input'\nimport { Select } from '../components/ui/select'\nimport { Dialog } from '../components/ui/dialog'\nimport { LoadingSpinner } from '../components/shared/LoadingSpinner'\nimport { EmptyState } from '../components/shared/EmptyState'\nimport { ErrorMessage } from '../components/shared/ErrorMessage'\n\nconst stageColors: Record<string, string> = {\n  Contact: 'border-t-blue-500',\n  Opportunity: 'border-t-amber-500',\n  Proposal: 'border-t-violet-500',\n  Implementation: 'border-t-cyan-500',\n  Onboarding: 'border-t-green-500',\n  Live: 'border-t-emerald-500',\n  Validated: 'border-t-purple-500',\n}\n\nconst stageBadgeColors: Record<string, string> = {\n  Contact: 'bg-blue-500/20 text-blue-300',\n  Opportunity: 'bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-300',\n  Proposal: 'bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-300',\n  Implementation: 'bg-cyan-500/20 text-cyan-300',\n  Onboarding: 'bg-green-500/20 text-green-300',\n  Live: 'bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-300',\n  Validated: 'bg-purple-500/20 text-purple-300',\n}\n\n/** Sub-status colors for within-stage breakdown */\nconst subStatusColors: Record<string, string> = {\n  'Proposal Preparation': 'border-l-violet-400',\n  'Proposal Accepted': 'border-l-indigo-400',\n  'Waiting for Contract & Payment': 'border-l-fuchsia-400',\n}\n\nconst subStatusBadgeColors: Record<string, string> = {\n  'Proposal Preparation': 'bg-violet-500/15 text-violet-300',\n  'Proposal Accepted': 'bg-indigo-500/15 text-indigo-300',\n  'Waiting for Contract & Payment': 'bg-fuchsia-500/15 text-fuchsia-300',\n}\n\nconst stageOrder = ['Contact', 'Opportunity', 'Proposal', 'Implementation', 'Onboarding', 'Live', 'Validated']\n\nexport default function ProjectsPage() {\n  const [showDialog, setShowDialog] = useState(false)\n  const [dragOverStage, setDragOverStage] = useState<string | null>(null)\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const { data: projects, isLoading, error } = useProjects()\n  const { data: people } = usePeople()\n  const createMutation = useCreateProject()\n  const stageMutation = useChangeProjectStage()\n  const deleteMutation = useDeleteProject()\n\n  const peopleByName = new Map((people || []).map((p) => [p.id, p.name]))\n\n  const groupedProjects: Record<string, any[]> = {}\n  for (const p of (projects || [])) {\n    if (!groupedProjects[p.stage]) groupedProjects[p.stage] = []\n    groupedProjects[p.stage].push(p)\n  }\n\n  const handleDelete = async (id: string) => {\n    if (confirm('Delete this project?')) await deleteMutation.mutateAsync(id)\n  }\n\n  // ── Drag & Drop handlers ──\n  const [dragOverSub, setDragOverSub] = useState<string | null>(null)\n\n  const handleDragStart = (e: React.DragEvent, projectId: string, currentStage: string, currentSub?: string | null) => {\n    e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', JSON.stringify({ id: projectId, stage: currentStage, subStatus: currentSub }))\n    e.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move'\n    const el = e.currentTarget as HTMLElement\n    requestAnimationFrame(() => { el.style.opacity = '0.5' })\n  }\n\n  const handleDragEnd = (e: React.DragEvent) => {\n    const el = e.currentTarget as HTMLElement\n    el.style.opacity = '1'\n    setDragOverStage(null)\n    setDragOverSub(null)\n  }\n\n  const handleDragOver = (e: React.DragEvent, stage: string) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    e.dataTransfer.dropEffect = 'move'\n    setDragOverStage(stage)\n  }\n\n  const handleDragLeave = (e: React.DragEvent) => {\n    // Only clear if actually leaving the column, not entering a child\n    const related = e.relatedTarget as HTMLElement | null\n    const col = e.currentTarget as HTMLElement\n    if (!col.contains(related)) {\n      setDragOverStage(null)\n      setDragOverSub(null)\n    }\n  }\n\n  const handleDrop = async (e: React.DragEvent, targetStage: string, targetSub?: string) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    setDragOverStage(null)\n    setDragOverSub(null)\n\n    try {\n      const data = JSON.parse(e.dataTransfer.getData('text/plain'))\n      if (data.stage !== targetStage) {\n        await stageMutation.mutateAsync({ id: data.id, stage: targetStage })\n      } else if (targetSub && data.subStatus !== targetSub) {\n        // Same stage, different sub-status\n        await stageMutation.mutateAsync({ id: data.id, stage: targetStage })\n        // Then update subStatus via REST (the PATCH above cleared it)\n        const res = await fetch(`/api/projects/${data.id}/substatus`, {\n          method: 'PATCH',\n          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n          body: JSON.stringify({ subStatus: targetSub }),\n        })\n        if (!res.ok) console.error('Sub-status update failed')\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      console.error('Drop failed:', err)\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Sub-status zones for Proposal column\n  const proposalSubStatuses = ['Proposal Preparation', 'Proposal Accepted', 'Waiting for Contract & Payment']\n\n  const getProjectsBySub = (projList: any[], sub: string) =>\n    projList.filter((p) => p.subStatus === sub)\n  const getProjectsWithoutSub = (projList: any[]) =>\n    projList.filter((p) => !p.subStatus)\n\n  if (isLoading) return <LoadingSpinner size=\"lg\" />\n  if (error) return <ErrorMessage />\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"space-y-4\">\n      <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n        <h1 className=\"text-xl font-bold text-[#e4e4ec]\">Projects</h1>\n        <Button onClick={() => setShowDialog(true)}>+ New Project</Button>\n      </div>\n\n      {(!projects || projects.length === 0) && <EmptyState message=\"No projects yet\" />}\n\n      <div className=\"flex gap-4 overflow-x-auto pb-4\" style={{ minHeight: 400 }}>\n        {stageOrder.map((stage) => {\n          const stageProjects = groupedProjects[stage] || []\n          const isDragOver = dragOverStage === stage\n          const isProposal = stage === 'Proposal'\n\n          const colContent = isProposal ? (\n            // ── Proposal column with sub-status zones ──\n            <div className=\"space-y-1 px-2 pb-2 min-h-[60px]\">\n              {/* Projects without sub-status */}\n              {getProjectsWithoutSub(stageProjects).map((p) => (\n                <ProjectCard\n                  key={p.id} p={p} peopleByName={peopleByName}\n                  onDragStart={handleDragStart} onDragEnd={handleDragEnd}\n                  onDelete={handleDelete} onNavigate={navigate}\n                  stageColors={stageColors} stage={stage}\n                />\n              ))}\n\n              {/* Sub-status zones */}\n              {proposalSubStatuses.map((sub) => {\n                const subProjs = getProjectsBySub(stageProjects, sub)\n                const isSubOver = dragOverSub === sub\n                return (\n                  <div\n                    key={sub}\n                    className={`rounded-md transition-colors duration-150 ${\n                      isSubOver ? 'bg-violet-500/10 ring-1 ring-violet-500/30' : ''\n                    }`}\n                    onDragOver={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); setDragOverSub(sub) }}\n                    onDragLeave={() => setDragOverSub(null)}\n                    onDrop={(e) => handleDrop(e, stage, sub)}\n                  >\n                    <div className=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2 py-1.5\">\n                      <span className={`text-[10px] font-medium px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded ${subStatusBadgeColors[sub] || ''}`}>\n                        {sub}\n                      </span>\n                      <span className=\"text-[10px] text-[#9898b0]\">{subProjs.length}</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div className=\"space-y-1.5 px-1 pb-1.5 min-h-[32px]\">\n                      {subProjs.map((p) => (\n                        <ProjectCard\n                          key={p.id} p={p} peopleByName={peopleByName}\n                          onDragStart={handleDragStart} onDragEnd={handleDragEnd}\n                          onDelete={handleDelete} onNavigate={navigate}\n                          stageColors={subStatusColors} stage={stage}\n                        />\n                      ))}\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                )\n              })}\n            </div>\n          ) : (\n            // ── Other columns — flat list ──\n            <div className=\"space-y-2 px-2 pb-2 min-h-[60px]\">\n              {stageProjects.map((p) => (\n                <ProjectCard\n                  key={p.id} p={p} peopleByName={peopleByName}\n                  onDragStart={handleDragStart} onDragEnd={handleDragEnd}\n                  onDelete={handleDelete} onNavigate={navigate}\n                  stageColors={stageColors} stage={stage}\n                />\n              ))}\n            </div>\n          )\n\n          return (\n            <div\n              key={stage}\n              className={`min-w-[260px] flex-shrink-0 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-150 ${\n                isDragOver ? 'bg-violet-500/10 ring-2 ring-violet-500/40' : ''\n              }`}\n              onDragOver={(e) => handleDragOver(e, stage)}\n              onDragLeave={handleDragLeave}\n              onDrop={(e) => handleDrop(e, stage)}\n            >\n              <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-2 px-3 pt-2\">\n                <span className={`text-xs font-semibold uppercase px-2 py-1 rounded ${stageBadgeColors[stage] || ''}`}>\n                  {stage}\n                </span>\n                <span className=\"text-xs text-[#9898b0]\">{stageProjects.length}</span>\n              </div>\n              {colContent}\n            </div>\n          )\n        })}\n      </div>\n\n      <ProjectFormDialog\n        open={showDialog}\n        onClose={() => setShowDialog(false)}\n        people={people || []}\n        onSave={async (data) => {\n          await createMutation.mutateAsync(data)\n          setShowDialog(false)\n        }}\n        loading={createMutation.isPending}\n      />\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// ── Project Card component ────────────────────────\nfunction ProjectCard({ p, peopleByName, onDragStart, onDragEnd, onDelete, onNavigate, stageColors }: {\n  p: any\n  peopleByName: Map<string, string>\n  onDragStart: (e: React.DragEvent, id: string, stage: string, subStatus?: string | null) => void\n  onDragEnd: (e: React.DragEvent) => void\n  onDelete: (id: string) => void\n  onNavigate: (path: string) => void\n  stageColors: Record<string, string>\n  stage: string\n}) {\n  const borderColor = stageColors[p.subStatus] || stageColors[p.stage] || ''\n  return (\n    <div\n      draggable\n      onDragStart={(e) => onDragStart(e, p.id, p.stage, p.subStatus)}\n      onDragEnd={onDragEnd}\n      className={`bg-[#1a1a24] rounded-lg border border-[#2a2a3a] border-t-2 ${borderColor} p-3 cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing hover:border-violet-500/50 transition-colors select-none`}\n      onClick={() => onNavigate(`/projects/${p.id}`)}\n    >\n      <p className=\"text-sm font-medium text-[#e4e4ec] truncate\">{p.name}</p>\n      <p className=\"text-xs text-[#9898b0] mt-1\">{peopleByName.get(p.peopleId) || '—'}</p>\n      <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between mt-2\">\n        {p.value != null && (\n          <span className=\"text-xs font-medium text-green-400\">€{p.value.toLocaleString()}</span>\n        )}\n        <Button\n          variant=\"ghost\"\n          size=\"sm\"\n          className=\"ml-auto\"\n          onClick={(e) => { e.stopPropagation(); onDelete(p.id) }}\n        >\n          🗑️\n        </Button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction ProjectFormDialog({\n  open, onClose, people, onSave, loading,\n}: {\n  open: boolean\n  onClose: () => void\n  people: { id: string; name: string }[]\n  onSave: (data: { name: string; peopleId: string; value?: number | null; stage?: string }) => void\n  loading: boolean\n}) {\n  const [name, setName] = useState('')\n  const [peopleId, setPeopleId] = useState(people[0]?.id || '')\n  const [value, setValue] = useState('')\n  const [stage, setStage] = useState('Contact')\n\n  const handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    onSave({ name, peopleId, value: value ? parseFloat(value) : null, stage })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <Dialog open={open} onClose={onClose} title=\"New Project\">\n      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className=\"space-y-3\">\n        <Input placeholder=\"Project name\" value={name} onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)} required />\n        <Select value={peopleId} onChange={setPeopleId} options={people.map((p) => ({ label: p.name, value: p.id }))} />\n        <Input placeholder=\"Value (€)\" type=\"number\" value={value} onChange={(e) => setValue(e.target.value)} />\n        <Select value={stage} onChange={setStage} options={stageOrder.map((s) => ({ label: s, value: s }))} />\n        <div className=\"flex justify-end gap-2 pt-2\">\n          <Button type=\"button\" variant=\"outline\" onClick={onClose}>Cancel</Button>\n          <Button type=\"submit\" disabled={loading}>Create</Button>\n        </div>\n      </form>\n    </Dialog>\n  )\n}"}],"details":{"persistedDetailsTruncated":true,"originalDetailsBytesAtLeast":8193,"originalDetailKeys":["status","exitCode","durationMs","aggregated","cwd"],"status":"completed","cwd":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace","exitCode":0},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840482059}}
{"type":"message","id":"5583c86c","parentId":"caec131d","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:12.155Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the issue. Let me look at the Zod schema:\n\n```ts\nexport const CreateProjectBody = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(1),\n  description: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  stage: z.string().default('Contact'),\n  subStatus: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  value: z.number().positive().optional().nullable(),\n  peopleId: z.string(),\n});\n```\n\nAnd looking at the frontend's `ProjectFormDialog`, the `onSave` callback sends:\n```ts\n{ name, peopleId, value: value ? parseFloat(value) : null, stage }\n```\n\nWait, but the form also allows the user to not select a `peopleId`. Looking at the code carefully:\n\n```ts\nconst [peopleId, setPeopleId] = useState(people[0]?.id || '')\n```\n\nIf `people` is empty (no people in the database), `people[0]?.id` would be undefined, so `peopleId` would be `''` (empty string). But the schema says `peopleId: z.string()` without a `.min(1)`, so an empty string would pass Zod validation but might cause Prisma issues (foreign key constraint).\n\nBut wait, the real issue: let me look at the `useCreateProject` hook to see how it sends the data...\n\nActually, let me look at the frontend API layer and the hooks to see how it's sending the data. Let me also check what error the API is actually returning by looking at its logs.\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The 500 error happens when POSTing to `/api/projects`. Let me check:\n\n1. The `CreateProjectBody` schema has `z.string()` for `peopleId` - an empty string would pass\n2. The Prisma schema has `peopleId String` - it's required, not optional\n3. If `peopleId` is an empty string, Prisma would try to create a project with `peopleId: ''`, which wouldn't match any `People` record and would fail with a foreign key error\n\nBut wait, the frontend sets `peopleId` to `people[0]?.id || ''`, so if there are people, it would default to the first person. The issue might be different.\n\nLet me also check: the `description` field - the frontend doesn't send `description`, so that should be fine (optional). The `value` field is parsed as `parseFloat(value)`, which if `value` is empty string would give `NaN`, but then it's converted to `null` via `value ? parseFloat(value) : null`. But `NaN` is truthy! So if the value field is empty, `value ? parseFloat(value) : null` would evaluate to... `'' ? NaN : null` → `''` is falsy → returns `null`. That's fine.\n\nBut if value is \"0\", `\"0\" ? parseFloat(\"0\") : null` → `\"0\"` is truthy → returns `0`. And `z.number().positive()` says positive, but 0 is not positive. So a value of 0 would fail Zod validation.\n\nWait, but the user probably isn't setting value to 0. Let me focus on the most likely issue.\n\nThe most likely issue is that `peopleId` could be an empty string if there are no people in the database. Let me check the actual API error by looking at what the API process outputs. Let me see if I can capture its stderr/stdout.\n\nActually, another key thing: the API uses `CreateProjectBody.parse(request.body)` in the route handler. If Zod validation fails, it throws a `ZodError` which Fastify might not handle properly, leading to a 500 instead of a 400. But let's check if there's an error handler.\n\nLet me look at the API's main entry point and error handling.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_cdh5baL7vOfOaLHK49cn1139","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/index.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_6kNYdFtRdwhozSnYs8sv4592","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/app.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_NhXv51Qy6nKRQ9gh6HAe9810","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/lib/errors.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":4837,"output":985,"cacheRead":39936,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45758,"cost":{"input":0.008416380000000001,"output":0.0034278,"cacheRead":0.005790719999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.017634900000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840482061,"responseId":"69eec929-d6e7-453f-a227-9e68ec6a0431"}}
{"type":"message","id":"46a5317b","parentId":"5583c86c","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:15.092Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_cdh5baL7vOfOaLHK49cn1139","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { buildApp } from './app.js';\nimport { config } from './config.js';\n\nasync function main() {\n  const app = await buildApp();\n\n  try {\n    await app.listen({ port: config.port, host: '0.0.0.0' });\n    console.log(`🚀 Ensoria OS API running on :${config.port}`);\n  } catch (err) {\n    app.log.error(err);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n}\n\nmain();\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840515092}}
{"type":"message","id":"f01e4fc0","parentId":"46a5317b","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:15.092Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_6kNYdFtRdwhozSnYs8sv4592","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import Fastify from 'fastify';\nimport cors from '@fastify/cors';\nimport jwt from '@fastify/jwt';\nimport { config } from './config.js';\nimport { errorHandler } from './lib/errors.js';\nimport authPlugin from './plugins/auth.js';\n\n// Module routes\nimport authRoutes from './modules/auth/auth.routes.js';\nimport peopleRoutes from './modules/people/people.routes.js';\nimport projectsRoutes from './modules/projects/projects.routes.js';\nimport conversationsRoutes from './modules/conversations/conversations.routes.js';\nimport requirementsRoutes from './modules/requirements/requirements.routes.js';\nimport milestonesRoutes from './modules/milestones/milestones.routes.js';\nimport collaboratorsRoutes from './modules/collaborators/collaborators.routes.js';\nimport plansRoutes from './modules/plans/plans.routes.js';\nimport filesRoutes from './modules/files/files.routes.js';\nimport dashboardRoutes from './modules/dashboard/dashboard.routes.js';\nimport mcpPlugin from './modules/mcp/mcp.plugin.js';\n\nexport async function buildApp() {\n  const app = Fastify({ logger: true });\n\n  // Error handler\n  app.setErrorHandler(errorHandler);\n\n  // CORS\n  await app.register(cors, { origin: true });\n\n  // JWT\n  await app.register(jwt, { secret: config.jwtSecret });\n\n  // Auth decorator\n  await app.register(authPlugin);\n\n  // Routes\n  await app.register(authRoutes, { prefix: '/api/auth' });\n  await app.register(peopleRoutes, { prefix: '/api/people' });\n  await app.register(projectsRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(conversationsRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(requirementsRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(milestonesRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(collaboratorsRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(plansRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(filesRoutes, { prefix: '/api/projects' });\n  await app.register(dashboardRoutes, { prefix: '/api/dashboard' });\n\n  // MCP Server\n  await app.register(mcpPlugin);\n\n  // Health check\n  app.get('/health', async () => ({ status: 'ok', service: 'ensoria-os' }));\n\n  return app;\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840515092}}
{"type":"message","id":"e884ff16","parentId":"f01e4fc0","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:15.093Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_NhXv51Qy6nKRQ9gh6HAe9810","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { FastifyError, FastifyReply, FastifyRequest } from 'fastify';\n\nexport class AppError extends Error {\n  constructor(\n    public statusCode: number,\n    public code: string,\n    message: string,\n    public details?: unknown,\n  ) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = 'AppError';\n  }\n}\n\nexport class NotFoundError extends AppError {\n  constructor(resource: string) {\n    super(404, 'NOT_FOUND', `${resource} not found`);\n  }\n}\n\nexport class ValidationError extends AppError {\n  constructor(message: string, details?: unknown) {\n    super(400, 'VALIDATION_ERROR', message, details);\n  }\n}\n\nexport class UnauthorizedError extends AppError {\n  constructor(message = 'Unauthorized') {\n    super(401, 'UNAUTHORIZED', message);\n  }\n}\n\nexport class ConflictError extends AppError {\n  constructor(message: string) {\n    super(409, 'CONFLICT', message);\n  }\n}\n\nexport function errorHandler(\n  error: FastifyError | AppError | Error,\n  _request: FastifyRequest,\n  reply: FastifyReply,\n) {\n  if (error instanceof AppError) {\n    return reply.status(error.statusCode).send({\n      error: {\n        code: error.code,\n        message: error.message,\n        ...(error.details ? { details: error.details } : {}),\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Fastify validation errors\n  if ('validation' in error && error.validation) {\n    return reply.status(400).send({\n      error: {\n        code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR',\n        message: 'Request validation failed',\n        details: error.validation,\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  console.error('Unhandled error:', error);\n  return reply.status(500).send({\n    error: {\n      code: 'INTERNAL_ERROR',\n      message: 'Internal server error',\n    },\n  });\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840515092}}
{"type":"message","id":"5f95c87e","parentId":"e884ff16","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:41.482Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue more clearly. The error handler in `errors.ts` catches `AppError`, Fastify validation errors, and then falls through to a generic 500. But Zod errors from `CreateProjectBody.parse()` are NOT `AppError` and NOT Fastify validation errors — they're `ZodError` instances. When `CreateProjectBody.parse(request.body)` fails, it throws a ZodError, which hits the catch-all 500 handler.\n\nBut the real question is: WHY is the Zod validation failing? Let me look at the Zod schema again:\n\n```ts\nexport const CreateProjectBody = z.object({\n  name: z.string().min(1),\n  description: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  stage: z.string().default('Contact'),\n  subStatus: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n  value: z.number().positive().optional().nullable(),\n  peopleId: z.string(),\n});\n```\n\nAnd the frontend sends:\n```ts\n{ name, peopleId, value: value ? parseFloat(value) : null, stage }\n```\n\nThere are a few possible issues:\n1. `peopleId` could be empty string `\"\"` if there are no people — and `z.string()` allows empty strings by default\n2. The `value` issue with `NaN` — but we already checked that\n3. The Zod v4 import — `z.number().positive()` — let me check Zod v4's API\n\nWait! The import is `import { z } from 'zod/v4'`. In Zod v4, the API changed. Let me check if `z.number().positive()` works in Zod v4. Also, `z.string().optional().nullable()` — in Zod v4, `.nullable()` might not exist or might work differently.\n\nHmm, but the actual error is a 500. The most likely cause is that Zod v4's `parse()` throws an error that the error handler doesn't catch properly. Let me check what version of Zod is installed and if there's a mismatch.\n\nActually wait, let me look at the package.json again. It says `\"zod\": \"^4.4.2\"`. And the import is `from 'zod/v4'`. If Zod v4 has breaking changes from v3, the schema might not work correctly.\n\nBut let me focus: the 500 error means the error handler's catch-all path is being hit. The error is either:\n1. A ZodError from validation (most likely)\n2. A Prisma error (foreign key, etc.)\n3. Something else\n\nLet me check what's actually happening. Let me try to authenticate and send a request with valid data to see the error.\n\nActually, I should check if there are even any people in the database. If the people list is empty, `people[0]?.id || ''` would be `''` and that would cause a foreign key error.\n\nLet me check the database and also look at what's being sent more carefully.\n\nWait, I should also check if the API has a middleware that adds `authenticate` to routes. If the authentication is failing and returning 401 (not 500), then the user is authenticated. So the issue is definitely in the project creation itself.\n\nLet me look at the frontend's `useProjects.ts` hook and `api.ts` to see the actual request.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_EPBcQLqNbqRYyorFYnl65301","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-ui/src -name \"useProjects.ts\" -exec cat {} \\; 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_OK4A5RosnfYgEp20BYvk0949","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-ui/src -name \"api.ts\" -exec cat {} \\; 2>/dev/null","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1125,"output":870,"cacheRead":45696,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47691,"cost":{"input":0.0019575,"output":0.0030276,"cacheRead":0.0066259199999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01161102}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840515093,"responseId":"c15ef5bc-4bad-467d-a70f-53709e220fd9"}}
{"type":"message","id":"85debb43","parentId":"5f95c87e","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:44.378Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_EPBcQLqNbqRYyorFYnl65301","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { useQuery, useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { get, post, put, patch, del } from '../lib/api'\n\nexport interface Project {\n  id: string\n  name: string\n  description?: string | null\n  stage: string\n  value?: number | null\n  peopleId: string\n  subStatus?: string | null\n  people?: { id: string; name: string; company?: string | null }\n  createdAt: string\n  updatedAt: string\n  conversations?: unknown[]\n  requirements?: unknown[]\n  milestones?: unknown[]\n  collaborators?: unknown[]\n  plans?: unknown[]\n  files?: unknown[]\n  analytics?: unknown[]\n}\n\nexport function useProjects(filters?: { stage?: string; peopleId?: string; search?: string }) {\n  const params = new URLSearchParams()\n  if (filters?.stage) params.set('stage', filters.stage)\n  if (filters?.peopleId) params.set('peopleId', filters.peopleId)\n  if (filters?.search) params.set('search', filters.search)\n  const qs = params.toString()\n\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['projects', filters],\n    queryFn: () => get<Project[]>(`/projects${qs ? `?${qs}` : ''}`),\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useProject(id: string) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['projects', id],\n    queryFn: () => get<Project>(`/projects/${id}`),\n    enabled: !!id,\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useCreateProject() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: (body: Partial<Project>) => post<Project>('/projects', body),\n    onSuccess: () => qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }),\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useUpdateProject() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: ({ id, ...body }: Partial<Project> & { id: string }) =>\n      put<Project>(`/projects/${id}`, body),\n    onSuccess: () => { qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }) },\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useDeleteProject() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: (id: string) => del(`/projects/${id}`),\n    onSuccess: () => qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }),\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useChangeProjectStage() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: ({ id, stage }: { id: string; stage: string }) =>\n      patch<Project>(`/projects/${id}/stage`, { stage }),\n    onSuccess: () => { qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }) },\n  })\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2012,"aggregated":"import { useQuery, useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { get, post, put, patch, del } from '../lib/api'\n\nexport interface Project {\n  id: string\n  name: string\n  description?: string | null\n  stage: string\n  value?: number | null\n  peopleId: string\n  subStatus?: string | null\n  people?: { id: string; name: string; company?: string | null }\n  createdAt: string\n  updatedAt: string\n  conversations?: unknown[]\n  requirements?: unknown[]\n  milestones?: unknown[]\n  collaborators?: unknown[]\n  plans?: unknown[]\n  files?: unknown[]\n  analytics?: unknown[]\n}\n\nexport function useProjects(filters?: { stage?: string; peopleId?: string; search?: string }) {\n  const params = new URLSearchParams()\n  if (filters?.stage) params.set('stage', filters.stage)\n  if (filters?.peopleId) params.set('peopleId', filters.peopleId)\n  if (filters?.search) params.set('search', filters.search)\n  const qs = params.toString()\n\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['projects', filters],\n    queryFn: () => get<Project[]>(`/projects${qs ? `?${qs}` : ''}`),\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useProject(id: string) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['projects', id],\n    queryFn: () => get<Project>(`/projects/${id}`),\n    enabled: !!id,\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useCreateProject() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: (body: Partial<Project>) => post<Project>('/projects', body),\n    onSuccess: () => qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }),\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useUpdateProject() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: ({ id, ...body }: Partial<Project> & { id: string }) =>\n      put<Project>(`/projects/${id}`, body),\n    onSuccess: () => { qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }) },\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useDeleteProject() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: (id: string) => del(`/projects/${id}`),\n    onSuccess: () => qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }),\n  })\n}\n\nexport function useChangeProjectStage() {\n  const qc = useQueryClient()\n  return useMutation({\n    mutationFn: ({ id, stage }: { id: string; stage: string }) =>\n      patch<Project>(`/projects/${id}/stage`, { stage }),\n    onSuccess: () => { qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] }) },\n  })\n}","cwd":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840544378}}
{"type":"message","id":"6c2bc12f","parentId":"85debb43","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:35:44.378Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_OK4A5RosnfYgEp20BYvk0949","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const API_BASE = '/api';\n\nfunction getToken(): string | null {\n  return localStorage.getItem('ensoria_token');\n}\n\nexport function setToken(token: string) {\n  localStorage.setItem('ensoria_token', token);\n}\n\nexport function removeToken() {\n  localStorage.removeItem('ensoria_token');\n}\n\nexport function getStoredToken(): string | null {\n  return getToken();\n}\n\nexport function isAuthenticated(): boolean {\n  return !!getToken();\n}\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const token = getToken();\n  const headers: Record<string, string> = {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    ...((options.headers as Record<string, string>) || {}),\n  };\n  if (token) headers['Authorization'] = `Bearer ${token}`;\n\n  const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}${path}`, { ...options, headers });\n  const json = await res.json();\n\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    const err = json.error || { code: 'UNKNOWN', message: 'Request failed' };\n    throw new Error(err.message);\n  }\n\n  return json.data;\n}\n\nexport function get<T>(path: string): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path);\n}\n\nexport function post<T>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n}\n\nexport function put<T>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'PUT', body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n}\n\nexport function patch<T>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n}\n\nexport function del<T>(path: string): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'DELETE' });\n}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2189,"aggregated":"const API_BASE = '/api';\n\nfunction getToken(): string | null {\n  return localStorage.getItem('ensoria_token');\n}\n\nexport function setToken(token: string) {\n  localStorage.setItem('ensoria_token', token);\n}\n\nexport function removeToken() {\n  localStorage.removeItem('ensoria_token');\n}\n\nexport function getStoredToken(): string | null {\n  return getToken();\n}\n\nexport function isAuthenticated(): boolean {\n  return !!getToken();\n}\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const token = getToken();\n  const headers: Record<string, string> = {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    ...((options.headers as Record<string, string>) || {}),\n  };\n  if (token) headers['Authorization'] = `Bearer ${token}`;\n\n  const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}${path}`, { ...options, headers });\n  const json = await res.json();\n\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    const err = json.error || { code: 'UNKNOWN', message: 'Request failed' };\n    throw new Error(err.message);\n  }\n\n  return json.data;\n}\n\nexport function get<T>(path: string): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path);\n}\n\nexport function post<T>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n}\n\nexport function put<T>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'PUT', body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n}\n\nexport function patch<T>(path: string, body: unknown): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n}\n\nexport function del<T>(path: string): Promise<T> {\n  return request<T>(path, { method: 'DELETE' });\n}","cwd":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777840544378}}
{"type":"message","id":"962f9d9d","parentId":"6c2bc12f","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:36:09.019Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture. The frontend sends:\n```ts\n{ name, peopleId, value: value ? parseFloat(value) : null, stage }\n```\n\nNow the issue could be:\n1. Zod v4 validation — the `parse()` call throws ZodError which gets caught by the generic 500 handler\n2. Prisma foreign key error if peopleId is empty\n\nLet me look at the actual error. Let me try to check the API's process output or find its log file. The API uses `Fastify({ logger: true })`, so it should log errors. Let me check if there's a way to see those logs.\n\nActually, let me try a different approach: let me look at what data the form actually sends by looking at the `onSave` callback more carefully.\n\nIn `ProjectsPage.tsx`:\n```tsx\nonSave={(data) => {\n  await createMutation.mutateAsync(data)\n  setShowDialog(false)\n}}\n```\n\nAnd `createMutation` is `useCreateProject()` which calls:\n```ts\nmutationFn: (body: Partial<Project>) => post<Project>('/projects', body),\n```\n\nAnd the data comes from `ProjectFormDialog`:\n```tsx\nconst handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    onSave({ name, peopleId, value: value ? parseFloat(value) : null, stage })\n  }\n```\n\nSo the body sent is: `{ name, peopleId, value: value ? parseFloat(value) : null, stage }`\n\nThe issue could be:\n1. `peopleId` is `\"\"` if people array is empty\n2. The Zod v4 schema `z.number().positive()` - if value is `null` and `.nullable()` is used, that should be fine\n3. Some other Zod v4 incompatibility\n\nLet me check if there are people in the database and also test the Zod schema directly.\n\nActually, let me just check the API logs more carefully. The Fastify logger might be outputting to somewhere.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_awLJHXCyuFF2IbxOq0lL5097","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if we can see the API server output - it might be running in a terminal\n# Let's check the Prisma database for people\ncd /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api && npx prisma db execute --stdin <<< \"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM People;\" 2>&1 | tail -5","timeout":15}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_4eWHKaa4UyQMikQr2SKa9888","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Also check if Zod v4 parse has issues\ncd /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api && node -e \"\nconst { z } = require('zod/v4');\ntry {\n  const schema = z.object({\n    name: z.string().min(1),\n    description: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n    stage: z.string().default('Contact'),\n    subStatus: z.string().optional().nullable(),\n    value: z.number().positive().optional().nullable(),\n    peopleId: z.string(),\n  });\n  const result = schema.parse({ name: 'Test', peopleId: '', stage: 'Contact' });\n  console.log('OK:', JSON.stringify(result));\n} catch(e) {\n  console.log('ERROR:', e.message);\n}\n\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1126,"output":777,"cacheRead":47616,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49519,"cost":{"input":0.00195924,"output":0.00270396,"cacheRead":0.006904319999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01156752}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840544379,"responseId":"0e79eede-edab-45fc-980c-8c3c07ed0f55"}}
