{"type":"message","id":"a9eec0a6","parentId":"3110d8a5","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:36:20.199Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The Zod validation passes with `peopleId: \"\"` (empty string). And the Prisma query also ran successfully (but it didn't show the count output).\n\nSo the Zod schema accepts an empty string for `peopleId`. The problem is then likely that Prisma tries to create a project with `peopleId: \"\"` which doesn't match any existing People record, causing a foreign key constraint error. Prisma errors would hit the catch-all 500 handler.\n\nOr the issue might be something else entirely. Let me try to actually reproduce the error. Let me authenticate and send a POST request.\n\nLet me first check if there are people in the database, and then try to create a project.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_rEo86lo7Vzdf02axvtA93199","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api && npx prisma db execute --stdin <<< \"SELECT id, name FROM People LIMIT 5;\" 2>&1 | tail -10","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":159,"output":251,"cacheRead":49408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49818,"cost":{"input":0.00027666,"output":0.00087348,"cacheRead":0.007164159999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0083143}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840572178,"responseId":"9385c087-ecaa-4b9c-b386-7f247f175a52"}}
