{"type":"message","id":"8cf4a4b7","parentId":"d0ed06e5","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:37:10.340Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. There are 2 people: Peter and Nicola. And there are users in the system. So the `peopleId` should not be empty — the dropdown in the form should show Peter and Nicola.\n\nBut let me think: when the form opens, `useState(people[0]?.id || '')` — the first person is Peter (cmops6jqj000hvrjt0hoefeli). So the default `peopleId` should be Peter's ID. Unless there's a race condition where `people` hasn't loaded yet when the dialog opens, or the `usePeople()` hook returns an empty array initially.\n\nActually, looking at the form more carefully:\n```tsx\nconst [peopleId, setPeopleId] = useState(people[0]?.id || '')\n```\n\nThis only initializes once when the component mounts. If `people` is empty at mount time, `peopleId` would be `''`. But wait — the `ProjectFormDialog` is only rendered when `showDialog` is true, and at that point `people` should already be loaded.\n\nHmm, but actually the dialog is rendered conditionally with `showDialog`, so `useState(people[0]?.id || '')` would run with the `people` array passed as prop at that moment, which should already be loaded.\n\nLet me try another approach: let me try to reproduce the error by calling the API.\n\nActually, I think I should just look at the Zod v4 issue more carefully. The import is `from 'zod/v4'` but the API might be using `z.coerce` or some v4-specific API that's different from v3.\n\nWait, let me re-check the Zod version and specifically test with the actual schema file.\n\nActually, I confirmed earlier that `schema.parse({ name: 'Test', peopleId: '', stage: 'Contact' })` works fine with Zod v4. So the Zod validation passes.\n\nThe 500 error must be coming from Prisma. Let me test by actually authenticating and sending a request.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_naVTTwQaeatA0bCZkWV83755","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Login and try creating a project\nTOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"email\":\"admin@ensoria.app\",\"password\":\"admin123\"}' | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('data',{}).get('token',''))\" 2>/dev/null)\n\necho \"Token: ${TOKEN:0:20}...\"\n\n# Try creating a project with empty peopleId (to test the 500 scenario)\necho \"--- Test with empty peopleId ---\"\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/projects \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"Test\",\"peopleId\":\"\",\"stage\":\"Contact\"}' 2>&1\n\necho \"\"\necho \"--- Test with valid peopleId ---\"\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/projects \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"Test2\",\"peopleId\":\"cmops6jqj000hvrjt0hoefeli\",\"stage\":\"Contact\"}' 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":191,"output":775,"cacheRead":50432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51398,"cost":{"input":0.00033234000000000003,"output":0.002697,"cacheRead":0.00731264,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01034198}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840605728,"responseId":"652f61b0-3804-4323-9375-b4b7147ddf52"}}
