{"type":"message","id":"4106c89d","parentId":"6f6224fd","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:39:58.457Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I've identified the issues:\n\n1. **Valid data works** — project created successfully.\n2. **Empty peopleId** → 500 — because Zod accepts `\"\"` but Prisma fails with foreign key error.\n3. **No peopleId** → 500 — Zod requires `peopleId` (it's not optional), so `CreateProjectBody.parse()` throws a ZodError → 500.\n4. **Value=0** → 500 — `z.number().positive()` rejects 0 (0 is not positive), so Zod throws → 500.\n\nThe root causes are:\n1. **ZodError not handled**: The error handler doesn't catch `ZodError` instances, so any Zod validation failure results in a 500 instead of a 400.\n2. **`peopleId` allows empty strings**: `z.string()` accepts empty strings, but Prisma needs a valid foreign key.\n3. **`z.number().positive()` rejects 0**: If user enters 0 as value, it fails validation.\n\nThe fixes needed:\n1. Add ZodError handling to the error handler → proper 400 responses\n2. Either: add `.min(1)` to `peopleId` in the schema, OR make `peopleId` optional and handle it in the service\n3. Change `z.number().positive()` to `z.number().min(0)` or handle the value=0 edge case\n\nBut most importantly, AleX's specific error — he's trying to create a project through the UI, which should be sending valid data (the form pre-selects Peter). Unless there's a different issue.\n\nWait, let me re-examine. He gets error `POST http://localhost:5173/api/projects 500`. The form sends `{ name, peopleId, value, stage }`. If the people list loaded correctly, `peopleId` should be Peter's ID. Unless...\n\nActually, let me also check: maybe the issue is that `usePeople()` returns an empty array initially and the dialog's `useState(people[0]?.id || '')` runs with `people = []` before the query resolves.\n\nLooking at the ProjectsPage:\n```tsx\nconst { data: people } = usePeople()\n// ...\n{showDialog && (\n  <ProjectFormDialog ... people={people || []} />\n)}\n```\n\nThe dialog is conditionally rendered. When `showDialog` becomes true, `ProjectFormDialog` mounts and `useState(people[0]?.id || '')` runs. By this time, `people` should be loaded from the query.\n\nBUT, React Query might return `undefined` initially while loading. If `usePeople()` returns `{ data: undefined, isLoading: true }`, then `people` would be `undefined`, and `people || []` would be `[]`. Then `people[0]?.id` would be `undefined`, and `peopleId` would be `''`.\n\nWait, but that wouldn't happen because the parent component has already rendered and the `people` data should be loaded by the time the user clicks \"New Project\".\n\nLet me check `usePeople` to see how it works.\n\nActually, let me focus on what we know: the 500 error happens. The most likely cause from the user's perspective is one of these:\n1. If he doesn't select a person from the dropdown and the default is empty\n2. If there's a ZodError from some field\n\nLet me just fix the underlying issues: the error handler, the Zod schema, and the peopleId validation. That will fix the root cause regardless of what exact scenario AleX is hitting.\n\nHere's my plan:\n1. Fix the error handler to catch ZodError → return 400 instead of 500\n2. Fix the `peopleId` schema to require `.min(1)` → empty string will fail validation with proper 400\n3. Fix the `value` schema from `.positive()` to `.min(0)` to accept 0\n\nActually wait, for the value, `z.number().positive()` means > 0. If the value is 0 in the form, it would trigger ZodError. But this is an edge case. The main issue is the ZodError not being handled.\n\nLet me also check if there could be other issues, like missing Prisma migrations or schema changes.\n\nActually, I just realized something: I successfully created a project with valid data. So the API works. The issue AleX is hitting must be a data issue. Let me check his localStorage to see what token he has and what data the form might be sending.\n\nBut I can't access browser localStorage from the command line. Let me just fix the known issues and explain to AleX what was happening.\n\nLet me fix:\n1. Error handler → add ZodError catch\n2. Schema → `peopleId: z.string().min(1)` and `value: z.number().min(0).optional().nullable()`\n3. Also consider adding `description` to the form data since the service expects it\n\nActually, looking at the form more carefully, it doesn't send `description`. The schema has `description: z.string().optional().nullable()`, so that's fine. But wait — the form sends `{ name, peopleId, value, stage }` which maps to `CreateProjectBody`. The schema has `description` as optional, so that's fine.\n\nLet me make the fixes now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Trovate le cause, AleX. Tre problemi che si combinano:\n\n1. **ZodError non gestito** — quando la validazione Zod fallisce, l'error handler restituisce un 500 generico invece di un 400 con messaggio chiaro\n2. **`peopleId` accetta stringa vuota** — `z.string()` senza `.min(1)` lascia passare `\"\"`, che poi Prisma rifiuta (foreign key)\n3. **`value: 0` bocciato da Zod** — `.positive()` rifiuta lo zero\n\nLa probabile causa nel tuo caso: il dropdown \"Person\" potrebbe non avere un valore selezionato di default quando apri la dialog.\n\nFaccio le fix:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_MgVWhctwnPthpIokBWad1413","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api/src/lib/errors.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"export function errorHandler(\n  error: FastifyError | AppError | Error,\n  _request: FastifyRequest,\n  reply: FastifyReply,\n) {\n  if (error instanceof AppError) {\n    return reply.status(error.statusCode).send({\n      error: {\n        code: error.code,\n        message: error.message,\n        ...(error.details ? { details: error.details } : {}),\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Fastify validation errors\n  if ('validation' in error && error.validation) {\n    return reply.status(400).send({\n      error: {\n        code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR',\n        message: 'Request validation failed',\n        details: error.validation,\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  console.error('Unhandled error:', error);\n  return reply.status(500).send({\n    error: {\n      code: 'INTERNAL_ERROR',\n      message: 'Internal server error',\n    },\n  });\n}","newText":"export function errorHandler(\n  error: FastifyError | AppError | Error,\n  _request: FastifyRequest,\n  reply: FastifyReply,\n) {\n  if (error instanceof AppError) {\n    return reply.status(error.statusCode).send({\n      error: {\n        code: error.code,\n        message: error.message,\n        ...(error.details ? { details: error.details } : {}),\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Fastify validation errors\n  if ('validation' in error && error.validation) {\n    return reply.status(400).send({\n      error: {\n        code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR',\n        message: 'Request validation failed',\n        details: error.validation,\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  // Zod validation errors\n  if (error.name === 'ZodError') {\n    const zodError = error as { issues?: Array<{ path: (string | number)[]; message: string }> };\n    return reply.status(400).send({\n      error: {\n        code: 'VALIDATION_ERROR',\n        message: 'Request validation failed',\n        details: zodError.issues?.map((i) => ({\n          path: i.path.join('.'),\n          message: i.message,\n        })),\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  console.error('Unhandled error:', error);\n  return reply.status(500).send({\n    error: {\n      code: 'INTERNAL_ERROR',\n      message: 'Internal server error',\n    },\n  });\n}"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":215,"output":2000,"cacheRead":64128,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66343,"cost":{"input":0.00037410000000000004,"output":0.00696,"cacheRead":0.009298559999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01663266}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timest