{"type":"message","id":"54a2da9a","parentId":"7ed8f2ae","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:40:42.895Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, all tests still return 500. The `tsx watch` might not have restarted, or the changes didn't take effect. Let me check if the API server process needs to be restarted manually. Or maybe there's a compilation/caching issue.\n\nActually wait, the issue might be that the error handler still isn't catching ZodError. Let me check what `ZodError` name looks like in Zod v4. In Zod v3, the error name is `ZodError`. But maybe in Zod v4 it's different?\n\nLet me check:\n1. Does `tsx watch` actually restart on file changes?\n2. What's the actual ZodError name in Zod v4?","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_UxI3G3thLJ1fzlWpgbyz6881","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check Zod v4 error name\ncd /Users/alessio/.openclaw/workspace/ensoria-api && node -e \"\nconst { z } = require('zod/v4');\ntry {\n  const schema = z.object({ name: z.string().min(1) });\n  schema.parse({});\n} catch(e) {\n  console.log('Error name:', e.name);\n  console.log('Error constructor:', e.constructor.name);\n  console.log('Message:', e.message);\n  console.log('Keys:', Object.keys(e));\n  console.log('Has issues:', !!e.issues);\n}\n\" 2>&1","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":189,"output":335,"cacheRead":67200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":67724,"cost":{"input":0.00032886,"output":0.0011658,"cacheRead":0.009744,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01123866}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777840832910,"responseId":"f1d1cca1-6ca8-4a08-bbcf-c6fcbd0314d4"}}
