{"type":"message","id":"1a62fc01","parentId":"091473fc","timestamp":"2026-05-03T20:44:17.071Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Same kind of issue - 500 error when trying to delete a project. Let me check the delete route and the projects service's remove function to see what's happening. Let me also check if the issue is that the project has related records (conversations, files, etc.) that might not be cascading properly, or maybe there's a ZodError or Prisma error.\n\nLooking at the code I already read:\n\nProjects routes:\n```ts\nfastify.delete('/:id', { onRequest: [fastify.authenticate] }, async (request) => {\n    const { id } = request.params as { id: string };\n    const data = await projectsService.remove(id);\n    return { data };\n  });\n```\n\nProjects service:\n```ts\nexport async function remove(id: string) {\n  await getById(id);  // throws NotFoundError if not found\n  await prisma.project.delete({ where: { id } });\n  return { success: true };\n}\n```\n\nThe Prisma schema has:\n```prisma\nmodel Project {\n  ...\n  conversations Conversation[]\n  files         ProjectFile[]\n  requirements  Requirement[]\n  milestones    Milestone[]\n  collaborators Collaborator[]\n  plans         ProjectPlan[]\n  analytics     AnalyticsRecord[]\n}\n```\n\nWith `onDelete: Cascade` on the relations. But wait, let me check `conversations`:\n\n```prisma\nmodel Conversation {\n  ...\n  project   Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n}\n```\n\nAnd `Activity` has:\n```prisma\nmodel Activity {\n  ...\n  peopleId    String?\n  people      People?  @relation(fields: [peopleId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  projectId   String?\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nNotice: `Activity` has `projectId` but NO relation to Project and NO `onDelete` cascade! If there's an Activity record with `projectId` pointing to the project being deleted, Prisma might throw a foreign key constraint error because there's no cascade defined.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the schema:\n\n```prisma\nmodel Activity {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  peopleId    String?\n  people      People?  @relation(fields: [peopleId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  projectId   String?\n  type        String   @default(\"created\")\n  description String\n  metadata    String?\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n}\n```\n\n`Activity` has `projectId` as a plain `String?` field WITHOUT a `@relation` to `Project`. In Prisma, this means there's NO foreign key constraint on Activity.projectId pointing to Project. So deleting a project wouldn't fail on Activity records.\n\nBut wait, when a project is created, the service creates an Activity:\n```ts\nif (data.peopleId) {\n    await prisma.activity.create({\n      data: {\n        peopleId: data.peopleId,\n        projectId: project.id,\n        type: 'created',\n        ...\n      },\n    });\n  }\n```\n\nSo there IS an Activity with `projectId`. But since there's no `@relation`, Prisma/SQLite wouldn't enforce a foreign key constraint. SQLite only enforces foreign keys if `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` is set, and Prisma might set that.\n\nActually, SQLite by default has foreign keys OFF. Prisma enables them via connection string parameter or pragma. Let me check the Prisma config.\n\nActually, the more important thing: let me just test the delete endpoint to see the actual error. Then I can see clearly what's happening.\n\nAlso, I notice the `errors.ts` change might not have caught the delete error because the API was restarted - actually wait, I did restart it. Let me test directly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_WGBu6mogdRZ5jwte029l2598","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"TOKEN=\"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1c2VySWQiOiJjbW9waDZjcDMwMDAwdGVqdHE3dmdjNGc1IiwiZW1haWwiOiJhZG1pbkBlbnNvcmlhLmFwcCIsInJvbGUiOiJhZG1pbiIsImlhdCI6MTc3Nzg0MDcxNn0.dSbhmf7HycSnb-s3Q65oS01rCa6gRgh4diSpEV-jnPw\"\n\necho \"=== Try delete ===\"\ncurl -s -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/projects/cmoq8gz5u000kxo1uoyfso8zx \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" 2>&1\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Try delete test project 4 ===\"\ncurl -s -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/projects/cmoq8k7i80000a6jt6btfop0r \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":30278,"output":1133,"cacheRead":32640,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64051,"cost":{"input":0.05268372,"output":0.00394284,"cacheRead":0.0047328,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06135936000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777841016327,"responseId":"19730411-186b-470c-9be7-d207ed8b5662"}}
