{"type":"message","id":"c12ed2cb","parentId":"3a45dbbb","timestamp":"2026-05-03T21:22:10.105Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looks clean! 254 files staged, properly filtered:\n- No `node_modules/` ✅\n- No `.env` ✅\n- No `memory/*.sqlite` files ✅\n- No OpenClaw runtime files (logs, browser, canvas, etc.) ✅\n- Workspace files, ensoria-api source, ensoria-ui source, config files ✅\n\nHowever, I notice some things that should maybe also be excluded:\n1. `workspace/state/` - runtime session state\n2. `workspace/.openclaw/workspace-state.json` - runtime state\n3. `workspace/google_token.json` - token file (but it's not in the list, so the gitignore caught it)\n4. `workspace/google_oauth_credentials.json` - credentials (also not in the list)\n\nThese look fine. The `.gitignore` is working.\n\nBut wait, there's also `openclaw.json` and `openclaw.yaml` being staged. These contain the OpenClaw config and might have API keys. Let me check if they contain sensitive data. But since AleX is committing to a local-only repo, this might be fine.\n\nActually, looking at the files staged, I also see the `openclaw.json.bak` files. These might contain old config with secrets. But they're in the root `~/.openclaw` so the `.gitignore` patterns would apply.\n\nLet me also check: `openclaw.json.bak` and `openclaw.json.bak.1` are staged. My .gitignore has `openclaw.json.*.bak` which should match `openclaw.json.bak`? Actually, the pattern `openclaw.json.*.bak` requires a dot before `bak`. `openclaw.json.bak` has `json.bak` not `json.*.bak`. Let me fix that.\n\nActually, looking more carefully: `openclaw.json.bak` matches `openclaw.json.bak` while the pattern `openclaw.json.*.bak` would match `openclaw.json.something.bak` but NOT `openclaw.json.bak` because there's no extra segment between `json` and `bak`.\n\nLet me fix the gitignore to also match `openclaw.json.bak` and `openclaw.json.bak.1`.\n\nActually, these are config files with potentially sensi